<h2>Las Cruces claim questions</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Is Mesilla covered if I live outside Las Cruces city limits?</summary><div class="a"><p>Yes. We serve properties throughout Doña Ana County, including Mesilla, Doña Ana and the outlying areas, as part of our statewide practice.</p></div></details><details><summary>My insurer says my roof was old and worn before the storm. Can appraisal help?</summary><div class="a"><p>If the disagreement is about how much storm damage occurred and what it costs to repair, appraisal is designed for that. If the carrier is denying coverage outright, that is a coverage question and you may want to consult a New Mexico attorney.</p></div></details><details><summary>Does the appraisal process cover my manufactured home?</summary><div class="a"><p>If your manufactured home policy contains an appraisal clause, it can generally be used the same way. The repair methods and pricing differ from site-built homes, so the scope needs to reflect how the home is actually built.</p></div></details></div>
